notes:Execution base: continue from accepted curator-spec candidate /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-2kp3tv/curator-spec-worktree and create a task-owned worktree/copy; preserve that predecessor read-only and do not stage, commit, publish, advance release pins, or claim platform validation. Define one closed v1 contract shared by local vendored and external-repository builds for Go, Rust, Swift, and Kotlin: manifest declares manager-defined toolchain id plus an explicit version constraint/compatibility requirement; manager policy alone resolves trusted executable paths and primary-source/platform remediation guidance. Package/repository data must not supply executable paths, download URLs, channels, package-manager/install commands, environment overrides, or trust roots. Host availability/version preflight must run before source acquisition or persistent mutation; source metadata compatibility cross-check runs only after local source validation or exact external acquisition+audit and before compiler work. Missing/unparseable/incompatible toolchain is an installation error with stable diagnostics and manager-owned recommendations; v1 never auto-installs. Resolved executable identity/version/target fingerprint must bind cache, receipt, marker/currentness semantics without changing frozen released artifacts. Include normative ordering, schemas/registry, positive+negative vectors, deterministic generation and release gates; keep skill-build.json as the sole neutral external descriptor.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-af7289, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-af7289)\nDelivered decision 0007 (canonical