codex
I found one review-blocking gap in the cycle-5 evidence probe: the `toolchain` command cross-check treats every unrecognized non-zero failure as “accepted.” That can hide a new upstream rejection layer or an unrelated command failure whenever the isolated parser says the name is representable, contradicting the contract’s claim that the two measurements catch drift independently. I’m pinning the exact evidence and will route this as research/decision rework, not a stop-the-line blocker.
